/*

1.
See screenshots folder.

2.
The (float *array) array has read access from multiple threads. Each thread reads a different part
of the array to calculate the histogram.

3.
The (partial_histograms) array has read and write access from multiple threads.
Each thread writes its own part of the array so there will not be any conflicting writes.
The main thread reads the partial histograms and combines them into a final histogram.

4.
Round Robin is suitable because it gives each thread cpu time 
and prevents one thread from using the cpu for too long.

Priority Scheduling can be unsuitable because lower priority threads 
can be starved if higher priority threads continuously use the cpu. 
This can delay the program because the main thread must wait for all worker threads to finish.


*/
